WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.930
- [Narrator] Let's say that
you have a jar of jelly beans,

00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:07.920
and you know that there
are exactly 282 jelly beans

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.970
in that jar of jelly beans.

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:12.850
And then the next day you come
and you see there are fewer

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:15.070
and you say, what happened,
and let's say someone

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:18.040
who lives with you or
your friend says, oh yeah,

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:23.040
I counted exactly and I ate
59 of those jelly beans.

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:28.340
So you started with 282, 59 are taken out,

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:31.630
and you don't need to know
exactly how many jelly beans

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:34.270
are left, but you wanna estimate roughly

00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:36.640
how many jelly beans are
left, and that's why,

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:38.460
as this title of the video says,

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:42.140
we're going to estimate when
subtracting large numbers.

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:44.360
And we can debate how large is large,

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:46.230
but these are reasonably large.

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:49.010
So let's do that, let's
see if we can estimate

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:52.420
what 282 minus 59 is.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:54.140
And sometimes when we're estimating,

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:56.920
we will use this squiggly equal sign.

00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:58.990
This means approximately,
which is another,

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:02.670
just a fancy way of saying
roughly what is this equal to.

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:05.680
So the way that I would
approach this, I would say hey,

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:10.260
are these close to numbers that
are easier to subtract with.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:14.730
So for example, 282,
I'd say, you know what,

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:17.830
maybe I can round to the nearest 10 here,

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:22.640
and so I could round it
down to 280, if I round down

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:23.473
to the nearest 10.

00:01:23.473 --> 00:01:27.490
If I rounded up, it would
be 290, but 282 is closer

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:30.420
to 280 than it is to 290.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:34.953
So I would round this,
when I'm estimating to 280.

00:01:36.265 --> 00:01:38.470
And then what about 59?

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:40.840
If I were to round to the nearest 10,

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:42.040
what would I round that to?

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:44.610
Pause the video and think about that.

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:47.790
Well, 59 if I round
down to the nearest 10,

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:50.190
it would be 50, and if I
round up to the nearest 10,

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:54.240
it would be 60, and 59 is
definitely closer to 60.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:57.110
So I would say that this is
roughly, if I'm rounding,

00:01:57.110 --> 00:01:59.570
I could say, hey I'm
gonna round that to 60.

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:03.930
So I could say the 282
minus 59 is roughly going

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:07.580
to be 280 minus 60.

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:08.700
And now what is this?

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:10.410
You might be able to do this in your head.

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:15.290
You could view this as
28 tens minus six tens,

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:18.410
and so if you have 28 of
something minus six of it,

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:21.770
you're going to be left
with 22 of that something.

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:25.270
And so you could say that
this is going to be 22 tens.

00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:28.400
22 tens, or another way to think about it.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:31.610
You have two 100s and then 8 tens,

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:33.500
and then you're gonna take
six tens away from it,

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:37.870
so then you'll be left
with two 100s and two tens.

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:39.410
Just like we have here.

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:41.290
So the whole point here, this is not,

00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:46.010
this is actually not exactly
what 282 minus 59 is,

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:49.730
but if you just said, hey
ballpark do I, I wanna know,

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:52.080
do I have roughly how many
jelly beans do I have,

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:53.650
well this could be useful.

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:55.260
And you'll see later in
life this is actually

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:57.120
a very, very usefully
skill where you might have

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:59.770
these numbers that get
a lot larger than this,

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:01.490
but you'll round to the nearest 10,

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:03.110
or you'll round to other places,

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:05.983
so that you can do that
computation in your head.

